 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "bava_metzia.94a.15",
   "daf": "94a",
   "sentenceId": 14,
   "he": "הֲדַרַן עֲלָךְ הַשּׂוֹכֵר אֶת הַפּוֹעֲלִים.",
   "en": ""
  },
  {
   "id": "bava_metzia.94a.16",
   "daf": "94a",
   "sentenceId": 15,
   "he": "מַתְנִי׳ הַשּׁוֹאֵל אֶת הַפָּרָה וְשָׁאַל בְּעָלֶיהָ עִמָּהּ, אוֹ שָׂכַר בְּעָלֶיהָ עִמָּהּ, שָׁאַל הַבְּעָלִים אוֹ שְׂכָרָן וְאַחַר כָּךְ שָׁאַל אֶת הַפָּרָה וָמֵתָה – פָּטוּר, שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר: ״אִם בְּעָלָיו עִמּוֹ לֹא יְשַׁלֵּם״.",
   "en": "«MISHNA:» In the case of «one who borrowed a cow and borrowed» the services of «its owner with it, or» he borrowed a cow and «hired its owner with it,» or he «borrowed» the services of «the owner or hired him and afterward borrowed the cow;» in all such cases, if the cow «died,» the borrower is «exempt» from liability. Although a borrower is generally liable to pay if a cow he borrowed dies, here he is exempt, «as it is stated: “If its owner is with him, he does not pay”» (Exodus 22:14)."
  },
  {
   "id": "bava_metzia.94b.1",
   "daf": "94b",
   "sentenceId": 0,
   "he": "אֲבָל שָׁאַל אֶת הַפָּרָה וְאַחַר כָּךְ שָׁאַל אֶת הַבְּעָלִים, אוֹ שְׂכָרָן, וָמֵתָה – חַיָּיב, שֶׁנֶּאֱמַר: ״בְּעָלָיו אֵין עִמּוֹ שַׁלֵּם יְשַׁלֵּם״.",
   "en": "«But» if one first «borrowed the cow and» only «afterward borrowed» the services of «the owner or hired him, and» the cow «died,» he is «liable» to pay the owner for the cow. This is the halakha even if the owner was working for the borrower at the time, «as it is stated: “If its owner is not with him, he shall pay”» (Exodus 22:13)."
  }
 ],
